{
  "id": "stop-signal-task",
  "term": "stop-signal task",
  "definition": "The stop-signal task is a cognitive task used to study response inhibition by having a person begin a response to a go signal and sometimes try to stop that response when a later stop signal appears. Performance reflects a race between the go process and the stop process, so stopping becomes harder when the stop signal comes later.",
